{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"New Jersey maximum security deposit","requirement":"A landlord may not collect a security deposit exceeding one and one-half times one month's rent, and any yearly increase in the deposit may not exceed 10% of the current deposit.","key_value":"1.5 months' rent; annual increase max 10%","coverage_conditions":"Residential rentals in New Jersey, including prepaid funds held to secure future rent such as last month's rent.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2","quoted_span":"The maximum-security deposit to be collected by the landlord cannot be more than one and one-half times one month’s rent ( N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2 ). It can be less. Any additional yearly security deposit increase may not exceed 10% of the current security deposit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit trust, holding and interest","requirement":"A security deposit remains the tenant's property and must be held in trust, not commingled; interest or earnings belong to the tenant and must be paid in cash or credited to rent on the lease renewal or anniversary, or on January 31 with written notice.","key_value":"interest paid on renewal/anniversary or January 31","coverage_conditions":"Residential rentals in New Jersey; landlords holding deposits for ten or more units may invest in approved New Jersey accounts.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"Does not apply to security deposits for seasonal use or rental of not more than 125 consecutive days.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-19","quoted_span":"The interest or earnings paid on the security deposit belongs to the tenant and shall be paid to the tenant in cash or credited toward rent due and owing on the ren ewal or anniversary of the tenant’s lease or on January 31,  if the tenant has been given written notice, that the interest payments will be paid on January 31 of each year (N.J.S.A. 46:8-19 (c)).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit notice and tenant rent-credit remedy","requirement":"Within 30 days of receiving a deposit and at each annual interest payment, the landlord must notify the tenant in writing of the banking institution, deposit amount, account type and interest rate; if this notice or the interest is withheld, the tenant may apply the deposit plus 7% interest to rent.","key_value":"30 days; 7% per annum","coverage_conditions":"All residential security deposits in New Jersey.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"Tenant may apply the security deposit plus interest at 7% per annum to rent after written notice and 30 days to comply.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-19.1","quoted_span":"Within 30 days of receipt of the security deposit and at t he time of each annual interest payment, the landlord must notify the tenant in writing of the name and address of the banking institution or investment company in which the money is deposited, the amount of the deposit, type of account, and current rate o f interest for the account.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit return and double-damage penalty","requirement":"A landlord must return the deposit plus interest, less itemized deductions, within 30 days after the tenancy ends, or within five business days if the tenant is displaced by fire, flood, condemnation or evacuation; a landlord who fails may owe double the amount wrongfully withheld.","key_value":"30 days; 5 business days if displaced","coverage_conditions":"All residential tenancies in New Jersey; for a broken lease the 30-day clock starts when the unit is re-rented or the lease expires, whichever is first.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"Court may award double the amount wrongfully withheld plus court costs and reasonable attorney's fees.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.1","quoted_span":"Within 30 days after the termination of a tenancy, a landlord must return the security deposit, plus interest earned less deductions, to the tenant ( N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.1).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit return after Safe Housing Act termination","requirement":"If a tenant ends a lease under the Safe Housing Act, the landlord must make the security deposit plus interest available within 15 business days and tell the tenant within three business days when and where to collect it.","key_value":"15 business days","coverage_conditions":"Tenants who terminate a lease under the New Jersey Safe Housing Act; does not apply to transient or seasonal rentals.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"Transient or seasonal rentals.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-9.6","quoted_span":"Within 15 business days after the lease  is terminated, the landlord shall make available the return of the tenant’s security deposit, plus any interest earned, to the tenant or the tenant’s agent.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
